      <div class="msl-container msl-reading-width">
        <p class="msl-eyebrow">Recognize the signs</p>
        <h2 id="problem-heading">Does This Sound Like a Main Sewer Problem?</h2>
        <p class="msl-intro">You do not need to diagnose the line before calling. These symptoms can point to a building drain or main sewer stoppage:</p>
        <ul class="msl-check-list">
          <li>More than one fixture slows, gurgles, or backs up at the same time.</li>
          <li>A toilet bubbles when another fixture drains.</li>
          <li>Water or sewage rises through a tub, shower, basement drain, or floor drain.</li>
          <li>The same backup returned after prior cleaning.</li>
          <li>A business has multiple restrooms or floor drains affected at once.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="msl-callout">Not sure whether it is a branch drain or the main line? Call and tell us what is backing up. We will ask a few quick questions before dispatch.</p>
      </div>
